From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:11:04 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 90/92] misc: modem_v1: wake the rmnet queues when the IPC link
 is reset

A CP crash stops the queues of the open rmnet devices, but resetting
the link after the CP's restart only cleared netif_stopped: rmnet0
kept its queue stopped (packets piling up in the qdisc) until the
interface went down and up. Wake them with the link.

(cherry picked from commit 9063f60e001428bf5d7752ea209435e1c49dfbca)
---
 drivers/misc/modem_v1/link_device_shmem.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/modem_v1/link_device_shmem.c b/drivers/misc/modem_v1/link_device_shmem.c
index a23384603..be1019fc0 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/modem_v1/link_device_shmem.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/modem_v1/link_device_shmem.c
@@ -151,6 +151,15 @@ static int shmem_reset_ipc_link(struct mem_link_device *mld)
 		dev->req_ack_cnt[RX] = 0;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A CP crash stopped the queues of the open rmnet devices
+	 * (stop_net_ifaces(), or vnet_xmit() while the CP was offline).
+	 * Downstream only cleared the flag here, so rmnet stayed stopped after
+	 * a CP restart until the interface was taken down and up again; wake
+	 * them with the link.
+	 */
+	if (ld->msd)
+		netif_tx_flowctl(ld->msd, false);
 	atomic_set(&ld->netif_stopped, 0);
 
 	set_magic(mld, MEM_IPC_MAGIC);
